#. Appended to the sync status when the failure carried a reason. The value is the server's or the network's own message and is not translated. Only the punctuation in front of it is: Chinese uses the full-width colon 「：」.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid ": {reason}"
msgstr "：{reason}"

#. The way out of [[Settings]], always back to the shelf because that is the only door in. The ‹ is part of the label. Shares its entry with the same button in the reader.
#. The way out of the reader, in the top bar. The ‹ is part of the label. 'Shelf' is the screen listing every book — the app's home.
#: src/components/Reader.tsx
#: src/components/SettingsScreen.tsx
msgid "‹ Shelf"
msgstr "‹ 本棚"

#. Stands in for the configured RP_ID in the message above when the deployment set none. Brackets included.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/rp-id.ts
msgid "auth.passkey.rpIdUnset"
msgstr "（未設定）"

#. On the banner naming the reader's place in the book: how long ago it was read. Whole days.
#: src/components/Reader.tsx
msgid "{count, plural, one {# day ago} other {# days ago}}"
msgstr "{count, plural, other {# 日前}}"

#. On the banner naming the reader's place in the book: how long ago it was read. Whole hours, under a day.
#: src/components/Reader.tsx
msgid "{count, plural, one {# hour ago} other {# hours ago}}"
msgstr "{count, plural, other {# 時間前}}"

#. On the banner naming the reader's place in the book: how long ago it was read. Whole minutes, under an hour.
#: src/components/Reader.tsx
msgid "{count, plural, one {# minute ago} other {# minutes ago}}"
msgstr "{count, plural, other {# 分前}}"

#. One half of the line under the typeface control, reporting which carried faces this device already holds. The value is a typeface name — 'Serif' or 'Sans' as translated elsewhere in this catalog. The two halves are joined with '・'.
#: src/components/TypographyForm.tsx
msgid "{face} is on this device"
msgstr "{face}はこの端末にあります"

#. One half of the line under the typeface control, reporting a carried face this device does not hold. The value is a typeface name — 'Serif' or 'Sans' as translated elsewhere in this catalog. The two halves are joined with '・'.
#: src/components/TypographyForm.tsx
msgid "{face} not downloaded yet"
msgstr "{face}はまだ未取得"

#. Second line under a book being read: how much reading is left, worked out from this reader's own pace. Half hours are common, so the number is 4.5 as often as it is 4.
#: src/lib/book-status.ts
msgid "{hours, plural, one {About # hour left} other {About # hours left}}"
msgstr "{hours, plural, other {残り約 # 時間}}"

#. The how-many-times number in the book-details panel, with its unit. A sitting is one continuous stretch of reading.
#: src/components/AboutBook.tsx
msgid "{sittings, plural, one {# sitting} other {# sittings}}"
msgstr "{sittings, plural, other {# 回}}"

#. Shown after the code has been sent, above the box it goes in. The value is the address the reader typed. Ten minutes is what the Worker actually enforces, so the number is not a rounding.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "A code is on its way to {email}. It is good for 10 minutes."
msgstr "{email} にコードを送りました。10 分間有効です。"

#. Refusal when codes are asked for too quickly. The value is how long is left to wait.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/auth.ts
msgid "auth.code.tooSoon"
msgstr "さきほどコードを送ったばかりです。{seconds} 秒後にお試しください"

#. Tooltip on the disabled columns control. It is disabled because frond cannot lay a vertically-written book out in two columns at all.
#: src/components/TypographyForm.tsx
msgid "A vertical book is always one column"
msgstr "縦組みの本は常に一段組みです"

#. Screen-reader name for the ⋯ button beside a book, which opens the panel holding everything else that book can do. The value is the book's own title.
#. Screen-reader name for the ⋯ button beside a book, which opens the panel holding everything else that book can do. The value is the book's own title.
#: src/components/Library.tsx
msgid "About {title}"
msgstr "{title} の詳細"

#. Screen-reader name for the button in the reader's bar that opens the panel describing the open book.
#. Title of the book-details panel, used only in the moment before the book itself has loaded — after that the panel wears the book's own title. Shares its entry with the reader's bar button that opens it.
#: src/components/AboutBook.tsx
#: src/components/Reader.tsx
msgid "About this book"
msgstr "この本について"

#. [[Settings]] tab holding sign-in, billing and backup.
#: src/components/SettingsScreen.tsx
msgid "Account"
msgstr "アカウント"

#. Button that registers another passkey on this account — one per device, so this is how a second machine gets a key. 'passkey' is the platform's own term; keep it as the platform spells it in this language.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "Add a passkey"
msgstr "パスキーを追加"

#. Button under a marked passage with no note yet: opens an empty note box.
#: src/components/Reader.tsx
msgid "Add note"
msgstr "メモを書く"

#. The button that grants the agent access to the shelf.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/authorize.ts
msgid "authorize.consent.approve"
msgstr "許可する"

#. Heading of the free half of the price list.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "Always free"
msgstr "ずっと無料"

#. Shown when the reader arrived here from an agent's authorisation flow rather than by choosing to sign in. It explains why they are looking at a login box, and that they will be sent back afterwards.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "An app wants to connect to your shelf. You will come back here to confirm after signing in."
msgstr "あるアプリがあなたの本棚に接続しようとしています。サインインすると、ここに戻って確認できます。"

#. Tooltip and screen-reader name for the ↻ button at the top right of the shelf's card. Draws a different marked passage onto the card. Not a refresh and not a dismissal — the reader is asking, and nothing is being cleared.
#: src/components/Library.tsx
msgid "Another passage"
msgstr "別の一節"

#. Refusal shown when a code is submitted for an address that was never sent one.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/auth.ts
msgid "auth.code.none"
msgstr "先にサインインコードを取り寄せてください"

#. One of three column choices for a page: let the line length decide how many columns fit.
#: src/lib/settings.ts
msgid "Auto"
msgstr "自動"

#. Screen-reader name for the ← in the corner of a panel covering the screen the reader was on, which is the arrangement on a hand-held. It dismisses the panel and returns them to what was underneath — the same thing Android's own back button does here.
#: src/components/Panel.tsx
msgid "Back"
msgstr "戻る"

#. Screen-reader name for the mark on the scrubber standing at the place the reader had read to, while they are back visiting a passage somewhere else. Pressing it takes them to that place. The value is a whole number. Longer than the words printed on it, which are only the number: what a glance gets from the mark's position on the rail has to be said out loud here.
#. placeholder {0}: mark.pct
#: src/components/Scrubber.tsx
msgid "Back to {0}%"
msgstr "{0}% に戻る"

#. Heading of the backup section in the account pane: one file out, the same file back in.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "Backup"
msgstr "バックアップ"

#. Heading of the billing section in the account pane.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "Billing"
msgstr "料金"

#. First of six line-height choices, and not a height at all: it means 'leave whatever the book asked for'. Same wording as the first typeface choice, which means the same thing — they share one entry deliberately.
#. One of three typeface choices, and the default: leave the fonts the book itself asked for. Short because the three sit side by side in a panel about a phone-width wide — Chinese says 書籍預設, which is narrower than English can be here.
#: src/lib/settings.ts
msgid "Book's"
msgstr "本のまま"

#. Button on the selection bar: drop the selection without marking anything.
#: src/components/Reader.tsx
msgid "Cancel"
msgstr "やめる"

#. Toast shown when every face the reader picked failed to arrive. Informational rather than an error: the book still renders, in whatever face the machine has.
#: src/lib/web-font-store.ts
msgid "Cannot download the font right now — using the system font"
msgstr "いまはフォントを取得できません。システムのフォントで表示します"

#. Replaces the line reporting which faces are held, when the store could not be read at all. A full sentence, because it is the whole line.
#: src/components/TypographyForm.tsx
msgid "Cannot read this device's fonts."
msgstr "この端末のフォントを読み取れません。"

#. Button beside the code box that goes back a step, for a reader who typed the wrong address.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "Change email"
msgstr "メールアドレスを変える"

#. Screen-reader name for the ✕ in the corner of a panel standing beside the screen the reader was on, which is the arrangement on a desk. A verb: it is the action, not a label for the thing being shut.
#: src/components/Panel.tsx
msgid "Close"
msgstr "閉じる"

#. Label of the control choosing how many columns a page is set in.
#: src/components/TypographyForm.tsx
msgid "Columns"
msgstr "段組み"

#. Bar button raising the panel that lists the book's chapters. Same word as that panel's own title.
#. Title of the panel listing the book's chapters, and the label of the bar button that raises it.
#: src/components/Reader.tsx
msgid "Contents"
msgstr "目次"

#. Shown above the shelf when an epub the reader dropped in could not be read. The first value is the file's own name; the second is why, and may be a message from deeper in the importer.
#: src/components/Library.tsx
msgid "Could not import {name}: {reason}"
msgstr "{name} を読み込めませんでした：{reason}"

#. One of three theme choices: pale text on a dark page.
#: src/lib/settings.ts
msgid "Dark"
msgstr "ダーク"

#. Button in the book-details panel that opens the delete confirmation. Shares its entry with the confirming button inside that dialog.
#. Button under a marked passage: removes the mark and any note on it.
#. The button that actually deletes, inside the confirmation. Shares its entry with the button that opened the dialog.
#: src/components/AboutBook.tsx
#: src/components/Reader.tsx
msgid "Delete"
msgstr "削除"

#. Title of the delete confirmation. The value is the book's own title; the quotation marks around it are this language's — Chinese uses 「」.
#: src/components/AboutBook.tsx
msgid "Delete “{title}”?"
msgstr "「{title}」を削除しますか？"

#. Stands in for the commit hash in [[Settings]]'s footer when the app was built somewhere with no git checkout — a tarball, or the test image. Lower case: it sits in a line of machine detail, not a heading.
#: src/lib/version.ts
msgid "dev build"
msgstr "開発版"

#. Button that closes the note box under a marked passage. The words are already written down by the time it is pressed — this only puts the box away — so it says the writing is finished rather than naming a save.
#: src/components/Reader.tsx
msgid "Done"
msgstr "完了"

#. Shown in place of the book when its epub could not be fetched and the failure carried no reason of its own.
#: src/components/Reader.tsx
msgid "Download failed"
msgstr "ダウンロードに失敗しました"

#. Shown to the reader when the epub file behind a book on the shelf could not be fetched. The value is the HTTP status code, kept because it is the one clue worth reporting.
#: src/lib/sync.ts
msgid "Download failed ({status})"
msgstr "ダウンロードに失敗しました（{status}）"

#. The running line in the typography panel while a CJK face downloads, when the server declared no total size so there is no percentage to show. The character between the words is an ideographic space (U+3000) — keep it, or use whatever spacing this language sets between a phrase and a figure.
#: src/lib/web-font-store.ts
msgid "Downloading font　{megabytes} MB"
msgstr "フォントを取得中　{megabytes} MB"

#. The running line in the typography panel while a CJK face downloads. The character between the words is an ideographic space (U+3000) — keep it, or use whatever spacing this language sets between a phrase and a figure.
#: src/lib/web-font-store.ts
msgid "Downloading font　{percent}%"
msgstr "フォントを取得中　{percent}%"

#. Stands in for the book while its epub is being fetched from the server. The ellipsis is one character.
#: src/components/Reader.tsx
msgid "Downloading the book…"
msgstr "本をダウンロード中…"

#. Button under a marked passage that already carries a note: opens it for changing.
#: src/components/Reader.tsx
msgid "Edit note"
msgstr "メモを直す"

#. Button that asks the server to email a one-time sign-in code. It is the first of the two doors in — the other is a passkey.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "Email me a code"
msgstr "コードをメールで送る"

#. Refusal when the sign-in form was submitted with no address at all.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/auth.ts
msgid "auth.email.missing"
msgstr "メールアドレスを入力してください"

#. Refusal when the verify request arrived without one of the two fields.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/auth.ts
msgid "auth.verify.missing"
msgstr "メールアドレスとコードの両方を入力してください"

#. Button that writes every book, note and position on this device out to one file.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "Export backup"
msgstr "バックアップを書き出す"

#. First line under a book the reader has read to the end.
#: src/lib/book-status.ts
msgid "Finished"
msgstr "読み終えた"

#. Label of the control choosing which face the book is set in. Kept short: the row is label-left, control-right, and the control beside it holds three options.
#: src/components/TypographyForm.tsx
msgid "Font"
msgstr "書体"

#. Screen-reader name for the progress bar shown while a CJK face downloads.
#: src/components/TypographyForm.tsx
msgid "Font download progress"
msgstr "フォントの取得状況"

#. The line in the typography panel when the face the book needs has already been downloaded, so choosing it costs nothing.
#: src/lib/web-font-store.ts
msgid "Font is on this device"
msgstr "フォントはこの端末にあります"

#. Eyebrow label at the top of the shelf's card, in front of the book's name. Says what the block is — a passage the reader marked, come back round. Lower case 'marks' is the same word the marking toolbar uses.
#: src/components/Library.tsx
msgid "From your marks"
msgstr "マークした一節から"

#. Button on the banner naming the reader's place in the book: moves the book to that place. Short — it sits beside 'Stay here'.
#: src/components/Reader.tsx
msgid "Go there"
msgstr "そこへ移動"

#. How long the code lasts. The value comes from what the Worker actually enforces, so it is not a rounded promise.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/email.ts
msgid "email.magicCode.validity"
msgstr "{minutes} 分間、一度だけ有効です。"

#. The half that matters: an account secured by email is only as strong as the inbox (ADR-0015). The advice is deliberately about the mailbox, not about Tidemarks.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/email.ts
msgid "email.loginNotice.wasNotYou"
msgstr "心当たりがない場合、あなたのメールを誰かが読める状態かもしれません。まずそのパスワードを変えてください。それがこのアカウントの本当の鍵です。"

#. The reassuring half of the sign-in notice.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/email.ts
msgid "email.loginNotice.wasYou"
msgstr "あなたご自身であれば、何もする必要はありません。"

#. Heading of the line explaining what happens if the reader stops paying.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "If you stop"
msgstr "やめたあと"

#. Closing line of the sign-in letter, for someone who did not ask for it. It says the code alone is the key, so ignoring the letter is enough.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/email.ts
msgid "email.magicCode.notYou"
msgstr "サインインしようとしていないなら、このメールは捨ててください。これがなければ誰も入れません。"

#. The shelf's own verb: opens a file picker for epub files. 'epub' stays lower case, as the format spells itself.
#: src/components/Library.tsx
msgid "Import epub"
msgstr "epub を読み込む"

#. What the free half covers. A list of the app's verbs, ending with where they run.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "Importing, reading, marking, note-taking, typesetting and exporting all run in your browser."
msgstr "読み込み、閲覧、マーク、メモ、組版、書き出しは、すべてブラウザの中で動きます。"

#. One of four ink colours for marking a passage. A pigment name, not a hue: the dye from the indigo plant (蓼藍).
#: src/lib/highlights.ts
msgid "Indigo"
msgstr "藍"

#. Tooltip on a quoted passage in the notes panel. Clicking it takes the reader to where that passage is in the book.
#: src/components/Reader.tsx
msgid "Jump to this passage"
msgstr "本文のこの位置へ"

#. Second line under a never-opened book. It answers 'so why is it here'.
#: src/lib/book-status.ts
msgid "Just added"
msgstr "追加したばかり"

#. How long ago the reader marked the passage showing on the shelf's card: within the hour. The card carries a distance rather than a date, because reaching back for what they were thinking then is what it is for.
#. On the banner naming the reader's place in the book: that place was read less than a minute ago. Also what a position written slightly in the future says, since two devices' clocks need not agree.
#: src/components/Library.tsx
#: src/components/Reader.tsx
msgid "Just now"
msgstr "たった今"

#. The way out of the delete confirmation: change nothing. Deliberately not 'Cancel' — it says what happens to the book, which is that it stays.
#: src/components/AboutBook.tsx
msgid "Keep it"
msgstr "残す"

#. The main button on the one book the reader is in the middle of. It reopens that book at the position they left.
#: src/components/Library.tsx
msgid "Keep reading"
msgstr "続きを読む"

#. Label of the only control in [[Settings]]'s language tab. The row beside it lists English / 繁體中文 / 日本語, each written in itself.
#. [[Settings]] tab holding the interface language. One word, sits beside Type and Account.
#: src/components/LanguageForm.tsx
#: src/components/SettingsScreen.tsx
msgid "Language"
msgstr "言語"

#. Widest of four margin widths.
#: src/lib/settings.ts
msgid "Large"
msgstr "広い"

#. How long ago the reader marked the passage showing on the shelf's card: one to two months back.
#: src/components/Library.tsx
msgid "Last month"
msgstr "先月"

#. How long ago the reader marked the passage showing on the shelf's card: one to two weeks back.
#: src/components/Library.tsx
msgid "Last week"
msgstr "先週"

#. How long ago the reader marked the passage showing on the shelf's card: one to two years back.
#: src/components/Library.tsx
msgid "Last year"
msgstr "去年"

#. The question on the consent page. The value is the name the agent registered under, and is escaped before it reaches the page. The quotation marks are this language's — Chinese uses 「」.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/authorize.ts
msgid "authorize.consent.heading"
msgstr "「{clientName}」を本棚に接続しますか？"

#. One of three theme choices: dark text on a pale page.
#: src/lib/settings.ts
msgid "Light"
msgstr "ライト"

#. Label of the line-height dropdown in the typography panel.
#: src/components/TypographyForm.tsx
msgid "Line height"
msgstr "行送り"

#. One of six line heights. The number is the multiplier and stays as it is.
#: src/lib/settings.ts
msgid "Loose (1.8)"
msgstr "ゆったり（1.8）"

#. One of six line heights. The number is the multiplier and stays as it is.
#: src/lib/settings.ts
msgid "Looser (2.0)"
msgstr "より広い（2.0）"

#. Widest of six line heights. The number is the multiplier and stays as it is.
#: src/lib/settings.ts
msgid "Loosest (2.2)"
msgstr "いちばん広い（2.2）"

#. Label of the margin control. It sets a floor for the whitespace along the line-length axis rather than the final width — see ADR-0012.
#: src/components/TypographyForm.tsx
msgid "Margin"
msgstr "余白"

#. Button on the selection bar: mark the passage and open a note on it in one action, rather than marking and then reopening it to write.
#: src/components/Reader.tsx
msgid "Mark and note"
msgstr "マークしてメモ"

#. Name of one of the four ink swatches on the selection bar. The value is a pigment name — Indigo, Ochre, Moss or Soot as translated elsewhere in this catalog.
#: src/components/Reader.tsx
msgid "Mark in {ink}"
msgstr "{ink}でマーク"

#. One of four margin widths, and the default.
#: src/lib/settings.ts
msgid "Medium"
msgstr "ふつう"

#. One of four ink colours for marking a passage. A pigment name: the green of moss (苔綠).
#: src/lib/highlights.ts
msgid "Moss"
msgstr "苔色"

#. Screen-reader name for one of the two page buttons flanking the book on a desk. Which side is 'next' flips for a right-opening book, so the two are chosen by direction rather than by position.
#. Screen-reader name for one of the two page buttons flanking the book on a desk. Which side is 'next' flips for a right-opening book, so the two are chosen by direction rather than by position.
#: src/components/Reader.tsx
msgid "Next page"
msgstr "次のページ"

#. The button that refuses the agent. Short and plain — it is the safe answer, not an apology.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/authorize.ts
msgid "authorize.consent.deny"
msgstr "しない"

#. Opening line of the account pane, before any mention of signing in. It is the product's own line: reading needs no account at all.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "No account needed to read. Your books, notes and reading positions never leave this device."
msgstr "読むだけならアカウントは要りません。本もメモも読書位置も、この端末から出ていきません。"

#. The whole of an empty shelf. Two short sentences: what is true, then what to do about it. It sits under the 'Import epub' button, so it points at that.
#: src/components/Library.tsx
msgid "No books yet. Drop an epub in, and start here."
msgstr "まだ本がありません。epub を置けば、ここから始まります。"

#. The anti-phishing line in the sign-in letter. Keep it blunt — its whole job is to be remembered by a reader who is being talked to by an attacker.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/email.ts
msgid "email.magicCode.warning"
msgstr "Tidemarks の者がこのコードをたずねることは決してありません。たずねてくる相手がいれば、それは私たちではありません。"

#. Smallest of four margin widths: no margin at all.
#: src/lib/settings.ts
msgid "None"
msgstr "なし"

#. Slotted into the import failure message below when the failure carried no reason of its own. Lower case, mid-sentence.
#: src/components/Library.tsx
msgid "not a valid epub file"
msgstr "有効な epub ファイルではありません"

#. First line under a book on the shelf that has never been opened.
#: src/lib/book-status.ts
msgid "Not opened yet"
msgstr "まだ開いていない"

#. Sync status beside the 'Sync' button: there is no account to sync with.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "Not signed in"
msgstr "未サインイン"

#. Placeholder in the empty note box under a marked passage. The ellipsis is one character.
#: src/components/Reader.tsx
msgid "Note…"
msgstr "メモ…"

#. Title of the panel listing what the reader has marked in this book, and the label of the bar button that raises it.
#: src/components/Reader.tsx
msgid "Notes"
msgstr "メモ"

#. Button that writes this book's marks and notes out as a Markdown file. '.md' is the file extension and stays as it is.
#: src/components/AboutBook.tsx
msgid "Notes .md"
msgstr "メモ .md"

#. Bar button raising the panel that lists what the reader has marked. The number in brackets is how many marks this book carries.
#: src/components/Reader.tsx
msgid "Notes ({markCount})"
msgstr "メモ（{markCount}）"

#. Stands where a marked passage would be, on a shelf that has books but nothing marked in any of them. It says what the slot is for rather than that it is empty.
#: src/components/Library.tsx
msgid "Nothing marked yet. A passage you mark while reading comes back to you here."
msgstr "まだ何もマークしていません。読みながらマークした一節が、ここに戻ってきます。"

#. Toast shown once a downloaded face has been applied to the book. The value is a typeface name — 'Serif' or 'Sans' as translated elsewhere in this catalog.
#: src/lib/web-font-store.ts
msgid "Now set in {familyLabel}"
msgstr "{familyLabel}を適用しました"

#. One of four ink colours for marking a passage. A pigment name: red earth (赭石).
#: src/lib/highlights.ts
msgid "Ochre"
msgstr "代赭"

#. Sync status beside the 'Sync' button: there is no network, which is not an error — reading carries on.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "Offline"
msgstr "オフライン"

#. The whole body of the consent page. It is HTML: keep the <strong> tags around whatever carries the emphasis in this language, and keep the three bullet lines starting with '  · '. The first bullet is the one that matters — an agent reads the books themselves, not merely their titles.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/authorize.ts
msgid "authorize.consent.body"
msgstr "接続すると、次のものを読み取れます：\n"
"\n"
"  · 本棚にあるすべての本（本文を含む）\n"
"  · どこまで読んだか、いま開いているページ\n"
"  · マークした箇所と書いたメモ\n"
"\n"
"書き換えることは<strong>できません</strong>。本を削除することもできません。Tidemarks からいつでも取り消せます。"

#. One column to a page. The word is a count of columns, not the digit.
#: src/lib/settings.ts
msgid "One"
msgstr "一段"

#. Second line under a book opened exactly once, in place of an estimate there is not enough reading to make.
#: src/lib/book-status.ts
msgid "Only just started"
msgstr "読みはじめたばかり"

#. Tooltip on a book's cover. The value is the book's own title and is never translated.
#. Tooltip on a book's cover. The value is the book's own title and is never translated.
#: src/components/Library.tsx
msgid "Open {title}"
msgstr "{title} を開く"

#. Label in front of the shelf's order dropdown. A noun, not the verb 'to sort'.
#: src/components/Library.tsx
msgid "Order"
msgstr "並び"

#. Heading of the paid half of the price list.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "Paid"
msgstr "有料"

#. Screen-reader name for one of the two page buttons flanking the book on a desk. Which side is 'previous' flips for a right-opening book, so the two are chosen by direction rather than by position.
#. Screen-reader name for one of the two page buttons flanking the book on a desk. Which side is 'previous' flips for a right-opening book, so the two are chosen by direction rather than by position.
#: src/components/Reader.tsx
msgid "Previous page"
msgstr "前のページ"

#. Label of the how-far number in the book-details panel. The value beside it is a percentage.
#: src/components/AboutBook.tsx
msgid "Read to"
msgstr "読んだところ"

#. Where the reader stopped, under a book on the shelf. The value is the chapter's own name, taken from the book — it is in the book's language and is never translated. It already carries whatever space this language wants in front of it (`leadingGap` in this file), so do not add one after the last word.
#: src/lib/book-status.ts
msgid "Read to {chapter}"
msgstr "{chapter}{gap}まで読んだ"

#. Where the reader stopped, under a book whose position could not be named as a chapter. The value is a whole number.
#: src/lib/book-status.ts
msgid "Read to {percent}%"
msgstr "{percent}% まで読んだ"

#. Screen-reader name for the scrubber, the bar along the edge of the book showing how far in the reader is.
#: src/components/Scrubber.tsx
msgid "Reading progress"
msgstr "読書の進み"

#. One of two ways to order the shelf, in a control beside 'Title'. Touched rather than read: half of what this order does is float freshly imported books, which nobody has read yet. The glossary calls it [[Last touched]], deliberately not 「最近閱讀」.
#: src/lib/shelf-order-choices.ts
msgid "Recently touched"
msgstr "最近さわった順"

#. Button under the typography controls. Puts all six settings back to what Tidemarks ships with. Disabled when they already are.
#: src/components/TypographyForm.tsx
msgid "Reset"
msgstr "初期値に戻す"

#. Shown when a backup file could not be read back in. The value is why, and may be a message from deeper in the parser.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "Restore failed: {reason}"
msgstr "復元に失敗しました：{reason}"

#. Button that reads a backup file back into this device. Deliberately not 'import' — that word belongs to adding an epub on the shelf.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "Restore from backup"
msgstr "バックアップから戻す"

#. One of three typeface choices for the book: a sans-serif face. In Chinese and Japanese this is a named style rather than a description — 黑體 / ゴシック体 — so use that name, not a translation of 'sans'.
#: src/lib/settings.ts
msgid "Sans"
msgstr "ゴシック体"

#. Screen-reader name for the draggable handle at the end of a passage the reader is selecting by touch. Dragging it moves that end of the selection.
#: src/components/SelectionLayer.tsx
msgid "Selection end"
msgstr "選択の終点"

#. Screen-reader name for the draggable handle at the beginning of a passage the reader is selecting by touch. Dragging it moves that end of the selection.
#: src/components/SelectionLayer.tsx
msgid "Selection start"
msgstr "選択の始点"

#. One of three typeface choices for the book: a serif face. In Chinese and Japanese this is a named style rather than a description — 明體 / 明朝体 — so use that name, not a translation of 'serif'.
#: src/lib/settings.ts
msgid "Serif"
msgstr "明朝体"

#. The one door out of the shelf, in the header beside the app's name. Opens [[Settings]].
#. Title of the settings screen. Shares its entry with the button on the shelf that opens it.
#: src/components/Library.tsx
#: src/components/SettingsScreen.tsx
msgid "Settings"
msgstr "設定"

#. Button that submits the code from the email and finishes signing in.
#. Heading of the sign-in section, shown when there is no account on this device yet.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "Sign in"
msgstr "サインイン"

#. Button that signs in with a passkey already on this device. 'passkey' is the platform's own term; keep it as the platform spells it in this language.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "Sign in with a passkey"
msgstr "パスキーでサインイン"

#. Button that ends the session on this device. Books already on the device stay; only the account link goes.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "Sign out"
msgstr "サインアウト"

#. Placeholder in the box the six-digit code from the email goes into.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "Sign-in code"
msgstr "サインインコード"

#. First line of the sign-in letter. The value is six digits.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/email.ts
msgid "email.magicCode.code"
msgstr "サインインコード：{code}"

#. Label of the how-many-times number in the book-details panel. A sitting is one continuous stretch of reading.
#: src/components/AboutBook.tsx
msgid "Sittings"
msgstr "回数"

#. Label of the font size slider, with the current value in it. The number is a percentage of the reader's own browser default, not a pixel size.
#: src/components/TypographyForm.tsx
msgid "Size {size}%"
msgstr "文字の大きさ {size}%"

#. One of four margin widths.
#: src/lib/settings.ts
msgid "Small"
msgstr "狭い"

#. First line of the after-the-fact sign-in notice.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/email.ts
msgid "email.loginNotice.body"
msgstr "あなたの Tidemarks アカウントに、コードでサインインがありました。"

#. One of four ink colours for marking a passage. A pigment name: lampblack ground from pine soot (松煙), the black of an ink stick.
#: src/lib/highlights.ts
msgid "Soot"
msgstr "松煙"

#. One of six line heights. The number is the multiplier and stays as it is.
#: src/lib/settings.ts
msgid "Standard (1.6)"
msgstr "標準（1.6）"

#. What to do about an unregistered app. The reader cannot fix it here, so it points them back at the thing that sent them.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/authorize.ts
msgid "authorize.unknownClient.body"
msgstr "お使いのエージェントから、もう一度接続してください。"

#. Button on the banner naming the reader's place in the book: makes the page on screen the reader's place, whatever the banner named. Short — it sits beside 'Go there'.
#: src/components/Reader.tsx
msgid "Stay here"
msgstr "ここに残る"

#. Button that runs a sync round now, rather than waiting for the next one. Same word as the section heading above it, and the same entry.
#. Heading of the section shown once the reader is signed in. It holds the sync status and the buttons for keys and signing out.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "Sync"
msgstr "同期"

#. What the monthly price is for: the two things that need a server.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "Sync and agents"
msgstr "同期とエージェント"

#. Sync status beside the 'Sync' button: the attempt reached the server and did not work.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "Sync failed"
msgstr "同期に失敗しました"

#. Sync status beside the 'Sync' button: this device and the server agree.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "Synced"
msgstr "同期済み"

#. What the paid half covers. Both are things that need a server, which is the whole reason they cost anything.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "Syncing between devices, and letting an agent read your books."
msgstr "端末どうしの同期と、エージェントから本を読めるようにすること。"

#. Sync status beside the 'Sync' button. The ellipsis is one character.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "Syncing…"
msgstr "同期中…"

#. One of three theme choices: follow whatever the operating system is set to.
#: src/lib/settings.ts
msgid "System"
msgstr "システムに合わせる"

#. Refusal when a passkey registration or sign-in took longer than the challenge stays valid. Nothing is wrong; the reader simply starts again.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/auth.ts
msgid "auth.passkey.challengeExpired"
msgstr "時間切れです。もう一度お試しください"

#. Refusal shown when the code is right but has been spent. Codes work once.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/auth.ts
msgid "auth.code.consumed"
msgstr "このコードはすでに使われています"

#. Refusal shown when the code is right but too old.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/auth.ts
msgid "auth.code.expired"
msgstr "コードの有効期限が切れています。もう一度取り寄せてください"

#. Refusal when the code simply does not match.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/auth.ts
msgid "auth.code.mismatch"
msgstr "コードが違います"

#. Refusal when the browser offered a passkey this deployment has never seen. Usually a key from another Tidemarks.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/auth.ts
msgid "auth.passkey.unknown"
msgstr "このパスキーは登録されていません"

#. Shown when the mail provider refused or was unreachable. Nothing is wrong with the reader's address; the failure is on this side.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/auth.ts
msgid "auth.code.sendFailed"
msgstr "コードを送れませんでした。しばらくしてからお試しください"

#. Slotted into the restore failure message below when the failure carried no reason of its own. Lower case, mid-sentence.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "the file is not in the right format"
msgstr "ファイルの形式が違います"

#. The line in the typography panel when the face this book wants is not held and cannot be fetched right now. It is a promise, not an error: the book still renders in the platform's own face.
#: src/lib/web-font-store.ts
msgid "The font will download once you are online"
msgstr "オンラインになったらフォントを取得します"

#. What happens if the reader stops paying. The point of the second sentence is that nothing on the device is held hostage (ADR-0013).
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "The server's copy is kept for 24 months. The books, notes and positions on this device are untouched."
msgstr "サーバー上の控えは 24 か月保管します。この端末の本・メモ・読書位置はそのままです。"

#. Label of the light/dark control in the typography panel.
#: src/components/TypographyForm.tsx
msgid "Theme"
msgstr "テーマ"

#. Heading of the consent page when the request itself is malformed and there is nowhere safe to redirect to.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/authorize.ts
msgid "authorize.badRequest.heading"
msgstr "この認可リクエストには問題があります"

#. Refusal shown while an allowlist is in force, before this deployment opens signups. Plain rather than vague on purpose: the person reading it is somebody the maintainer knows, and a vague answer would leave them watching an empty inbox.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/signup-gate.ts
msgid "signup.notYet"
msgstr "このメールアドレスはまだ登録できません"

#. Heading of the consent page when the agent's client id is unknown to this deployment.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/authorize.ts
msgid "authorize.unknownClient.heading"
msgstr "このアプリは登録されていません"

#. The whole of the notes panel when nothing has been marked in this book. Two short sentences: what is true, then what to do about it.
#: src/components/Reader.tsx
msgid "This book is unmarked. Select a passage to leave a mark."
msgstr "この本にはまだ何もありません。一節を選ぶと、しるしが残せます。"

#. The one thing a reader cannot see from the shelf, and the reason this question is asked at all: deleting takes the marks and notes with it, everywhere.
#: src/components/AboutBook.tsx
msgid "This book's marks and notes go with it, on your other devices too."
msgstr "この本のマークとメモも一緒に消えます。ほかの端末からも消えます。"

#. Tooltip on the build stamp in [[Settings]]'s footer, shown only when the '+' after the commit hash is there. It explains what that '+' means.
#: src/components/SettingsScreen.tsx
msgid "This build came from a working tree with uncommitted changes"
msgstr "このビルドは未コミットの変更がある作業ツリーから作られています"

#. Shown when a deployment's WebAuthn RP_ID does not cover the hostname the reader arrived on. Both names are in the sentence on purpose, so the mismatch and its fix are in one place. The first value is the configured RP_ID, or the words for 'not set' when there is none.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/rp-id.ts
msgid "auth.passkey.rpIdMismatch"
msgstr "この配備の RP_ID は {configured} ですが、いま接続しているのは {host} です。このアドレスではパスキーを使えません。メールのコードでサインインするか、配備の設定を直してください。"

#. Under the language control in [[Settings]]. Explains the two things a reader is most likely to wonder: whether this travels with the account, and whether it changes their books.
#: src/components/LanguageForm.tsx
msgid "This device only — the language follows the machine in your hand, not your account. Books are unaffected: each one is laid out in whatever it was written in."
msgstr "この端末だけの設定です。言語はアカウントではなく、手元の端末に従います。本には影響しません。どの本もそれぞれ書かれた言語のまま組まれます。"

#. Shown in place of the book when the epub is on the device but could not be parsed.
#: src/components/Reader.tsx
msgid "This file will not open"
msgstr "このファイルは開けません"

#. How long ago the reader marked the passage showing on the shelf's card: two to four weeks back.
#: src/components/Library.tsx
msgid "This month"
msgstr "今月"

#. Shown when one section of an otherwise readable book fails. The value is the renderer's own message and is not translated.
#: src/components/Reader.tsx
msgid "This section will not render: {reason}"
msgstr "この節は表示できません：{reason}"

#. How long ago the reader marked the passage showing on the shelf's card: two to seven days back.
#: src/components/Library.tsx
msgid "This week"
msgstr "今週"

#. How long ago the reader marked the passage showing on the shelf's card: two months to a year back.
#: src/components/Library.tsx
msgid "This year"
msgstr "今年"

#. Subject line of the letter carrying a one-time sign-in code. The product name stays as it is; the value is six digits.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/email.ts
msgid "email.magicCode.subject"
msgstr "Tidemarks サインインコード：{code}"

#. Subject of the letter sent after a successful code sign-in. The product name stays as it is.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/email.ts
msgid "email.loginNotice.subject"
msgstr "Tidemarks：コードでサインインがありました"

#. One of six line heights. The number is the multiplier and stays as it is.
#: src/lib/settings.ts
msgid "Tight (1.4)"
msgstr "つめる（1.4）"

#. Label of the total-reading-time number in the book-details panel.
#: src/components/AboutBook.tsx
msgid "Time spent"
msgstr "読んだ時間"

#. The other way to order the shelf: by the book's own title, collated for the interface language.
#: src/lib/shelf-order-choices.ts
msgid "Title"
msgstr "書名順"

#. How long ago the reader marked the passage showing on the shelf's card: earlier today.
#: src/components/Library.tsx
msgid "Today"
msgstr "今日"

#. Refusal after the guess limit. The code is dead rather than the account locked, so asking for a new one works.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/auth.ts
msgid "auth.code.locked"
msgstr "間違いが多すぎたため、このコードは無効になりました。もう一度取り寄せてください"

#. Two columns to a page, turned past together as one page.
#: src/lib/settings.ts
msgid "Two"
msgstr "二段"

#. Bar button raising the panel holding the six typography settings. Same word as that panel's own title.
#. Title of the panel holding the six typography settings, and the label of the bar button that raises it. It is about how the book is set, not about the book's contents.
#. [[Settings]] tab holding the six typography settings. Shares its entry with the reader's own bar button for the same panel.
#: src/components/Reader.tsx
#: src/components/SettingsScreen.tsx
msgid "Type"
msgstr "組版"

#. The monthly price. The figure is a placeholder and nothing charges yet, which the note below says outright.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "US$3 a month (provisional)"
msgstr "月 US$3（暫定）"

#. Refusal when a passkey could not be verified. Deliberately says nothing about why: which part failed is not something an attacker should be told.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: worker/auth.ts
msgid "auth.passkey.failed"
msgstr "検証に失敗しました"

#. Note under the billing section, pointing at the way out of paying: the syncing half is open source and can be run by the reader.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "Would rather not pay, but want two devices? The syncing half can be self-hosted."
msgstr "お金は払いたくないけれど端末を二台使いたい場合は、同期の側を自分で立てられます。"

#. How long ago the reader marked the passage showing on the shelf's card: more than two years, the far end of the scale. Vague on purpose — past a certain distance the exact count stops meaning anything.
#: src/components/Library.tsx
msgid "Years ago"
msgstr "数年前"

#. How long ago the reader marked the passage showing on the shelf's card: the day before.
#: src/components/Library.tsx
msgid "Yesterday"
msgstr "昨日"

#. Note under the billing section. It says outright that the section describes an intention, not a working checkout.
#: src/components/AccountPanel.tsx
msgid "You cannot subscribe yet, and the price is not settled."
msgstr "まだ購読はできません。価格も決まっていません。"

#. Banner over the book, naming the reader's place in it when that place is not what is on screen. The value is the chapter's own name, taken from the book — it is in the book's language and is never translated. The place was written somewhere else while this device had the book open, and the sentence does not say where on purpose: Tidemarks cannot tell which device wrote a position, or even whether it was another browser on this one.
#. placeholder {0}: elsewhere.position.chapterLabel
#: src/components/Reader.tsx
msgid "You were reading “{0}”"
msgstr "「{0}」まで読んでいます"

#. Banner over the book, naming the reader's place in it when that place is not what is on screen, and it cannot be named as a chapter. The value is a whole number. The place was written somewhere else while this device had the book open, and the sentence does not say where on purpose: Tidemarks cannot tell which device wrote a position, or even whether it was another browser on this one.
#. placeholder {0}: Math.round(elsewhere.position.percentage * 100)
#: src/components/Reader.tsx
msgid "You were reading at {0}%"
msgstr "{0}% まで読んでいます"
